## Build

```bash
# Release build
cargo build -p {crate-name} --release

# Cross-compile (if applicable)
cross build -p {crate-name} --release --target {target-triple}
```

## Package

| Artifact | Path | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `{binary}` | `target/release/{binary}` | {Main executable} |
| `{library}` | `target/release/lib{name}.rlib` | {Library artifact} |
| `{config}` | `deploy/{config-file}` | {Default configuration} |

## Publish

1. Ensure all CI checks pass on the release branch.
2. Tag the release: `git tag -a v{X.Y.Z} -m "{Release description}"`
3. Push the tag: `git push origin v{X.Y.Z}`
4. {Publish to crates.io / deploy container / copy artifact}
5. Verify the published artifact: `{verification command}`

## Rollback

1. Identify the last known-good version: `v{X.Y.Z}`
2. {Revert deployment / re-deploy previous tag / roll back migration}
3. Verify rollback: `{health check command}`
4. Open an incident report if rollback was triggered by a defect.

